{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/MatchingModule\/documentation\/MatchingModule","doc:\/\/MatchingModule\/documentation\/MatchingModule\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/MatchingModule\/documentation\/MatchingModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"maximumWeightBMatching"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"bipartition"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/BipartiteGraphs\/documentation\/BipartiteGraphs\/Bipartition","preciseIdentifier":"s:15BipartiteGraphs11BipartitionV","text":"Bipartition"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":">, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"capacity"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"weight"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","text":"Edges"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","text":"Index"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/MatchingModule\/documentation\/MatchingModule\/BMatching","preciseIdentifier":"s:14MatchingModule9BMatchingV","text":"BMatching"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SZ","text":"SignedInteger"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"parameters":[{"name":"bipartition","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The graph’s two sides."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"capacity","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"How many matched edges each vertex may have, at least zero."}]}]},{"name":"weight","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each edge’s weight by position."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"kind":"parameters"},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A minimum-cost circulation (the network simplex): a source feeds each left vertex up to its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"capacity, each edge of positive weight carries one unit at the cost of minus its weight,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"each right vertex drains into a sink up to its capacity, and the sink returns to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"source. Edges of weight zero or less are never taken. Parallel edges are distinct and may","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"both be taken. Which optimum is returned when several exist is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"unspecified, but the same input always gives the same result. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"capacity"},{"text":" is called once","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"per vertex in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"text":" order and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"weight"},{"text":" once per edge in position order.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Complexity","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"That of the network simplex on n + 2 vertices and n + m + 1 arcs; polynomial"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in practice, O(n² m) in the worst case of its pivots."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Precondition","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"code":"bipartition","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is this graph’s; every capacity is at least zero and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"capacities fit in ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; |weight| fits the network simplex’s cost bound (4(n + 3)(the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"greatest weight + 1) fits in ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The maximum-weight b-matching of a bipartite graph: the edges of greatest total weight,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each taken at most once, meeting each vertex "},{"code":"v","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" at most "},{"code":"capacity(v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" times."}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/MatchingModule\/documentation\/MatchingModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/maximumWeightBMatching(bipartition:capacity:weight:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/matchingmodule\/graphprotocols\/graph\/maximumweightbmatching(bipartition:capacity:weight:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P14MatchingModuleE22maximumWeightBMatching11bipartition8capacity6weightAD0G0Vyxqd__G15BipartiteGraphs11BipartitionV